            {
                "entry_id": "dbb7f107-d3d2-3b23-9ebf-ae38e57cf04f",
                "word": "omnicide",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "627dcfe1-fbe8-46b5-b218-8ed8d90544df",
                        "entry_id": "dbb7f107-d3d2-3b23-9ebf-ae38e57cf04f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "omnicides"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72552933-8f3b-31c8-aef6-4a10e5bf5512",
                        "entry_id": "dbb7f107-d3d2-3b23-9ebf-ae38e57cf04f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Destruction de toute forme de vie sur Terre causée par l’activité humaine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c32d116-4094-4c76-a563-a7ed24524c54",
                                "sense_id": "72552933-8f3b-31c8-aef6-4a10e5bf5512",
                                "text": "Les temps ont changé. Un ordre s’achève, bipolaire, fondé sur l’équilibre de la terreur et la hantise de l’omnicide nucléaire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73be48f7-7136-4e8b-8bd9-d5bc7de82c2f",
                                "sense_id": "72552933-8f3b-31c8-aef6-4a10e5bf5512",
                                "text": "Pendant ce temps, la vie publique est dominée par ce que Freud appelait le processus de répétition : le besoin d’une « maladie finale » (A. Rapaport) a trouvé un nouvel aliment dans plusieurs « omnicides » (J. Somerville et S. Shibata) : la guerre nucléaire mais également l’omnicide par la faim et l’écocide."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2b44b70-20e9-4204-9b48-df9e35bd95a8",
                                "sense_id": "72552933-8f3b-31c8-aef6-4a10e5bf5512",
                                "text": "Cette théorie a contribué à la prise de conscience que l’homme a la capacité de détruire son environnement naturel. À ce titre, le philosophe John Somerville a défini le concept d'« omnicide » (du latin omnis, « tout », et coedere, « tuer »), « pour exprimer la capacité meurtrière des armes nucléaires dans la mesure où ni le terme de “génocide” ni celui de “guerre nucléaire” n'expriment les capacités de destructions massives."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6d0214e-7d9a-411e-afc8-fce9dae53d2f",
                                "sense_id": "72552933-8f3b-31c8-aef6-4a10e5bf5512",
                                "text": "Dans une relative indifférence, la forêt californienne continue de partir en fumée. Ces derniers jours, pas moins de 8 000 kilomètres carrés (80 fois la surface de Paris) ont été ravagés par les flammes. Difficile de ne pas y voir un effet du réchauffement climatique, ce qui pousse certains à parler d’« omnicide » pour insister sur notre responsabilité collective dans ce « meurtre de toutes choses »."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e63cb404-8310-4f59-8936-e3bf1e3bec44",
                        "source_entry_id": "dbb7f107-d3d2-3b23-9ebf-ae38e57cf04f",
                        "source_sense_id": "72552933-8f3b-31c8-aef6-4a10e5bf5512",
                        "target_lang_word": "Omnizid",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d4764be9-30b1-497b-bfba-3f6110378e99",
                        "source_entry_id": "dbb7f107-d3d2-3b23-9ebf-ae38e57cf04f",
                        "source_sense_id": "72552933-8f3b-31c8-aef6-4a10e5bf5512",
                        "target_lang_word": "omnicide",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "omnicide",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51869afc-2c88-30d9-8a37-ba7cb3a72909",
                                        "entry_id": "0793ca3d-aa2a-3de6-bf20-72a327f13898",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The total extinction of the human species as a result of human action. Most commonly it refers to human extinction through nuclear warfare, but it can also refer to such extinction through other means such as global anthropogenic ecological catastrophe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85ab54a8-5d8f-4a6d-81de-196b4e3d37c6",
                                                "sense_id": "51869afc-2c88-30d9-8a37-ba7cb3a72909",
                                                "text": "How extraordinary that Curtis LeMay believed for the rest of his life that the United States “lost” the Cuban missile crisis and the Cold War. If John Kennedy had followed LeMay's advice [to bomb Cuba and take out the missile sites], history would have forgotten the Nazis and their terrible Holocaust. Ours would have been the historic omnicide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3da1af60-f07d-3577-a4d2-746dd084087f",
                                        "entry_id": "0793ca3d-aa2a-3de6-bf20-72a327f13898",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone or something that causes total destruction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d4faea9-8451-4191-ac2c-80a0530c8e7f",
                                                "sense_id": "3da1af60-f07d-3577-a4d2-746dd084087f",
                                                "text": "Our soils have been made sterile over many areas from pesticides, which have been really omnicides. Today, DDT as the greatest culprit, and one which has brought immense profit to the pesticide producing industry, has been spread worldwide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1d72889-87c0-4c2c-a122-b998cbbfaf5d",
                                                "sense_id": "3da1af60-f07d-3577-a4d2-746dd084087f",
                                                "text": "Ilmari? First name of a would-be Turkish papicide? A Libyan omnicide? No, merely that of an apparently mild-mannered Finn whose studies put him at the crossroads of the major influences so patently reflected in his music—those of Rachmaninoff and of the French Impressionists."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5ad1ebc-5570-47df-916b-e620fa72eda6",
                                                "sense_id": "3da1af60-f07d-3577-a4d2-746dd084087f",
                                                "text": "[T]hese ‘super-bombs’ shatter a civilisation’s own planet but ‘the nuclear jets from the explosion could even activate their Sun, transforming it into a giant hydrogen bomb’. Perhaps supernovas are twinkling omnicides in the sky."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
